   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3773"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dharmakīrti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi grags pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos grags</persName><birth notBefore="0550-01-01">after 550</birth><death notAfter="0660-12-31">before 660</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6120</idno><idno type="APIS">3773</idno><note type="comment">The dates 600-660 were proposed in [C7GN3X2Q].&#13;
The mid-sixth century for his birth date was proposed in [KQVXHPVH].</note></person><person xml:id="person3807"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre shes rab 'bar</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འབྲེ་ཤེས་རབ་འབར</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dre chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dre shes rab 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bri shes rab 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shes rab bla ma</persName><birth notBefore="1040-01-01" notAfter="1100-12-31">after 1040 before 1100</birth><death notAfter="1200-12-31">before 1200</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2274</idno><idno type="APIS">3807</idno><note type="comment">Further holy places associated to him are: Ze thang, Grwa thang and rMog po ([647FFPZR]: 545, based on [Q3KCZX7B]: 38).&#13;
Remembered for thirteen distinguished objects (such as royal insignia and religious articles), which could be objects of his clan ([4LDAV8UH]: 95.).</note></person><person xml:id="person3831"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phywa pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཕྱྭ་པ་ཆོས་ཀྱི་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi seng+ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya pa chos seng ge ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge' slong chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes chen po phya pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon phya pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon cha pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i dbang phyug phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i dbang phyug chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa chen po cha pa</persName><birth notBefore="1109-01-01" notAfter="1109-12-31">1109</birth><death notBefore="1169-04-23" notAfter="1169-04-23">1169-04-23</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1404</idno><idno type="APIS">3831</idno><note type="comment">The majority of the information available on Phya pa has been provided in [EZ5JXHJY] and [8S7FDMCJ]. Summaries of the same are also found in [LQZU66YX]: 37-40, [F4UK2S8P]: 2-3, and [BW9UR427]: 35-36 (in French).&#13;
&#13;
&#13;
On his birth in 1109, the year of rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786)'s passing, see [TM8DW8WA]: 32-33, [VKBZTBWN]: 4b4-5, and [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b2-3.&#13;
On the date of his passing in a "sa mo glang" year, see [R894SIKE]: 400, [VKBZTBWN]: 4b4-5 and 6a5. &#13;
[95UZA9Y5]: 40/3/5 (reported in [7FZ3B926]: 111 and [MPRU5QUC]: 206) specifies the day "sa mo glang gi lo'i nag pa zla ba nag po'i phyogs kyi tshes brgyad," i.e., on the 23rd of the third month.&#13;
&#13;
A list of his students is provided in [EZ5JXHJY]: 356, based on [MQB8JGAX]: 297/4, [KL9XTQWI]: I, 454, [4YEPFBIB]: 340-341, [8GL7ZT7Y], fol. 15b3, [VKBZTBWN], fol. 4b7-5a4.&#13;
[FDEWZ2NZ]: 290 also mentions the list of the four "jo sras" from bSod nams dpal's Bla ma rngog pa yab sras rim par byon pa’i rnam thar rin po che’i rgyan gyi phreng ba.&#13;
&#13;
'Gos lo tsa ba lists numerous works composed before Phya pa took the see of gSang phu; these include commentaries and summaries on the Five works of Maitreya, the Pramāṇaviniścaya, the Satyadvayavibhaṅga, Madhyamakālaṃkāra, Madhyamakāloka, and  Bodhicaryāvatāra. He mentions having seen these, the Yid kyi mun sel (ID:4503) and summaries on Madhyamaka, as well as (ID:4505) and (ID:5971). See exX0032026-04-2304-02-58 .&#13;
'Gos lo tsa ba does not mention any composition dealing with monastic discipline. &#13;
&#13;
Śākya mchog ldan ([TM8DW8WA], 12-13 and 32) mentions a (doubtful) commentary on the Pramāṇavārttika (ID:3772) in addition to the commentary on the Pramāṇaviniścaya, and three summaries (small, intermediate, large), the intermediate one being the Yid kyi mun sel (ID:4503). (Discussed in [EZ5JXHJY]: 357, translated in [8S7FDMCJ]: 59).&#13;
&#13;
Four groups of students are mentioned in Tibetan sources (which do not imply that the members of the respective groups were studying with Phya pa at the same time), with occasional variations:&#13;
&#13;
1) The "Eight Great Lions" (seng chen brgyad). Eight scholars whose names contains the expression "seng ge," likely connoting their expertise in epistemology. The standard list includes gTsang nag pa (ID:3839), Dan 'bag (ID:3840), 'Bru sha (ID:3841), rMa bya (ID:3842), rTsags/rTsegs (ID:4289), Myang/Nyang bran (ID:3844), and gNyal pa/dMyal ma (ID:6679). The eighth one is instead sometimes said to be gTsang pa 'Jam dpal (ID:6336), 'U yug pa (ID:3846), or mTshur ston (DI:4315).&#13;
&#13;
2) The "four sons of noble families" (jo sras mi bzhi) or the "three sons of noble families" (jo sras gsum). They are young noble men of the rNgog (ID:3847), 'Khon (ID:3848), Khu (ID:3849), and gNyos/sMyos (ID:3850). The four are listed in [VKBZTBWN]: 4a7 and [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b3, whereas on 16a1 the author speaks of "jo sras gsum." The four are also listed by bSod nams dpal, see [FDEWZ2NZ]: 290.&#13;
&#13;
3) The "three wise ones" (shes rab can mi gsum) or "four wise ones" (shes rab can mi bzhi). The threefold-list in [VKBZTBWN]: 5a1 has rKong po (ID:3852), lHo pa sgom gzan (ID:3853), Par bu ba/sPar phu ba (ID:3854). 'Gar dbang grub (ID:3851) is added in the fourfold list, e.g. in [R894SIKE]: 406.&#13;
&#13;
4) The "three accomplished ones" (grub thob mi gsum). These are students who later became famous masters: Dus gsum mkhyen pa (ID:3855), Phag mo gru pa (ID:3856), gSal sto (ID:3857). The third is sometimes replaced by Zhang tshal (ID:6409), or is suggested to be the latter's direct student.</note></person><person xml:id="person3839"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nag pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཙང་ནག་པ་བརྩོན་འགྲུས་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtson 'grus seng+ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags phug pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang nag</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon gtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa rtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge' slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags phug pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dbu ma smra ba'i dge' slong bstson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mang du thos pa'i dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs par smra ba'i dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon grags pa'i dbang phyug gtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">vīryasiṃha</persName><birth notAfter="1150-12-31">before 1150</birth><death notBefore="1195-01-01">after 1195</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2259</idno><idno type="APIS">3839</idno><note type="comment">Van der Kuijp ([H9MPLMTV]) proposed the dates (?-1185). The terminus ante quem for gTsang nag pa's death was pushed to 1192 by Schwabland ([Q8WU9EDW]: 794, n. 3) on account of the date of Khro pu lo tsA ba (ID:3878)'s studies with gTsang nag pa. This date was corrected to 1195 based on Khro phu lo tsA ba's biography (van der Kuijp, personal communication).</note></person><person xml:id="person4098"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rdo rje dbang grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྡོ་རྗེ་དབང་གྲགས</persName><birth notAfter="1267-12-31">before 1267</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4098</idno></person><person xml:id="person4099"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi bzhad pa</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཆོས་ཀྱི་བཞད་པ</persName><birth notBefore="1150-01-01">after 1150</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4099</idno><note type="comment">Lay follower of Buddhism (dge snyen).&#13;
A post-colophon annotation of instance (ID:5301) mentions a "shag kya'i dge bsnyen chos kyi blo gros," who might be the same person or a subsequent disciple.</note></person><person xml:id="person4293"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thod pa bsod nams seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཐོད་པ་བསོད་ནམས་སེང་གེ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4293</idno></person><person xml:id="person4593"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">Anonymous</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨཱནོཉམོཨུས</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4593</idno></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3772"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">pramāṇavārttika</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">pramāṇavārttikakārikā</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam 'grel gyi tshig le'ur byas pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rnam 'grel</title><date type="composition" notBefore="0560-01-01" notAfter="0660-12-31">after 560 before 660</date><author ref="person:3773">dharmakīrti</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">3772</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5302"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma'i de kho nyid bsdus pa nye bar bsdus pa ye shes rdo rje rin chen</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མའི་དེ་ཁོ་ཉིད་བསྡུས་པ་ཉེ་བར་བསྡུས་པ་ཡེ་ཤེས་རྡོ་རྗེ་རིན་ཆེན</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ye shes rdo rje rin po che</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma’i de kho na nyid bsdus pa nye bar bsdus pa</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1160-01-01">after 1160</date><author ref="person:4099">chos kyi bzhad pa</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Compendium of the author's bla ma (rdo rje dbang grags)'s work (ID: 5958).&#13;
The work postdates the contribution of gTsang nag pa (ID:3839), who is mentioned nominally on fol. 9a5 of (ID:5301). &#13;
It mentions the triad "bshad/'chzad/brtsod."</note><relatedItem type="commentaryOn" target="work:5958"/><respStmt><resp>prompter</resp><name ref="person:4293">thod pa bsod nams seng ge</name></respStmt><idno type="APIS">5302</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5958"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma sde bdun kyi de kho na nyid bsdus pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མ་སྡེ་བདུན་ཀྱི་དེ་ཁོ་ན་ཉིད་བསྡུས་པ</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1157-01-01" notAfter="1277-12-31">after 1157 before 1277</date><author ref="person:4098">rdo rje dbang grags</author><note type="isExtant">False</note><note type="comment">Date of composition: bde bar bshegs pa'i bstan pa lnga brgya' bdun pa la bab pa'i tshe | me mo glang gi lo = 1157, 1217, 1277...</note><idno type="APIS">5958</idno></bibl></listBibl><listPlace><place xml:id="place5718"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gte' ra bkra shis dbu mang gi dgon pa</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">གཏེའ་ར་བཀྲ་ཤིས་དབུ་མང་གི་དགོན་པ</placeName><idno type="APIS">5718</idno></place><place xml:id="place6060"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">g.yag rde</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">གཡག་རྡེ</placeName><idno type="APIS">6060</idno></place></listPlace><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel5107" name="quotes-without-name" active="#person4099" passive="#person3807" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex088052025-05-2615-57-58"/><ptr target="#ex088052025-05-2616-07-01"/><ptr target="#ex088052025-05-2616-02-05"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel5104" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person4099" passive="#person3831" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex088052025-05-2615-53-57"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel5106" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person4099" passive="#person3839" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex088052025-05-2615-53-11"/><ptr target="#ex088052025-05-2616-07-01"/><ptr target="#ex088052025-05-2616-12-23"/><ptr target="#ex088052025-